  "articleBody": "You're probably wondering, \"How long will I be without my bathroom?\" That's a super common question! The timeline for bathroom floor tile installation can vary, but for a smaller bathroom, it often wraps up in a few days to about a week. It's not just about laying the tile, though; there are several steps that each need their own time. First, there's the preparation phase – cleaning and leveling the subfloor, which can take a day or so depending on its condition. Then comes the actual tile setting. Once the tiles are down, you absolutely can't walk on them right away! Most installers will tell you to wait at least 24 hours for the mortar to cure properly. Rushing this step is a big no-no because it can cause tiles to shift or crack. After the initial curing, it's time for grouting. Grouting itself is quick, but then the grout also needs time to cure and harden, which can be another 24-72 hours before it's ready for light use, and even longer for full curing. So, while you might see a beautiful new floor quickly, the full process, including proper drying and curing times, typically means a few days of patience. For a clear estimate and a smooth process, always chat with your installer, like HH Remodeling LLC, who can give you a precise timeline based on your specific project.",
